  "result": "All five tests pass (`python -m pytest -q`, both test files).\n\nChanges, all in `netgraph/graph.py`:\n\n- **`remove_edge(u, v)`** discards `v` from `u`'s set and vice versa, decrements the edge counter, and returns whether the edge existed. The self-loop case works because the second discard is a no-op.\n- **`degree(u)`** returns the size of `u`'s neighbour set, so a self-loop naturally counts once.\n- **`connected_components()`** runs an iterative DFS from each unvisited node in ascending order. Scanning starts from 0 upward means components come out ordered by smallest node; each component is sorted before being appended. Isolated nodes form singleton components.\n\nAll three validate node ids with the existing `IndexError` check.",
